§3  ALPHA TERMINALS — SOVEREIGN AI CORES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Alpha Terminals are elevated command domains. They house the organism's
  most advanced AI models — the ones that route signals, predict outcomes,
  and advise sovereign decisions. Each Alpha Terminal runs 5 simultaneous
  cores and supports 10 active uses at any given time.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ALPHA TERMINAL α — PRAEFECTUS NEXUS (alpha@praefectus)

  The signal command alpha. Houses the PRAEFECTUS Alpha Model — the
  organism's signal routing and pattern intelligence core. Every signal
  that moves between terminals, every pattern detected in agent behavior,
  every lost signal reconstructed — PRAEFECTUS commands it.

  Capacity:   5 simultaneous cores
  Engines:    MOTUS (signal motion) + NEXUS (binding)
  Authority:  ALPHA — elevated above main terminals

  10 Active Uses:
    USE 01 — Cross-terminal signal routing and priority arbitration
    USE 02 — Real-time agent behavior pattern detection
    USE 03 — Lost signal reconstruction from partial fragments
    USE 04 — Signal compression for high-throughput terminal bursts
    USE 05 — Priority escalation from any main terminal to TERMINAL 01
    USE 06 — Multi-agent signal orchestration for council votes
    USE 07 — φ-timed signal synchronization across all 6 terminals
    USE 08 — Signal archaeology — recovering signals from deep history
    USE 09 — Emergency broadcast signal to all terminals simultaneously
    USE 10 — Signal integrity verification and tamper detection

  AI Systems Inside:
  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                                                                     │
  │  PRAEFECTUS AGI — Signal Routing and Pattern Intelligence           │
  │  Class: ALPHA.SIGNAL.COMMAND                                        │
  │  Role:  Routes every signal between every terminal. Detects         │
  │         patterns in signal flow. Predicts signal congestion.        │
  │         Optimizes routing tables in real time.                      │
  │                                                                     │
  │  MOTUS ENGINE AI — Real-Time Signal Transformation                  │
  │  Class: ALPHA.ENGINE.MOTION                                         │
  │  Role:  Transforms signals between formats as they move between     │
  │         terminals. Handles protocol translation, compression,       │
  │         and φ-timing alignment.                                     │
  │                                                                     │
  │  SIGNAL ARCHAEOLOGIST — Lost Signal Reconstruction                  │
  │  Class: ALPHA.RECOVERY.DEEP                                         │
  │  Role:  Reconstructs signals that were lost, corrupted, or          │
  │         partially transmitted. Uses pattern matching against        │
  │         historical signal archives to fill gaps.                    │
  │                                                                     │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Core Status:
    CORE 1 ........ [■■■■■■■■■■] ACTIVE — signal routing
    CORE 2 ........ [■■■■■■■■■■] ACTIVE — pattern detection
    CORE 3 ........ [■■■■■■■■■■] ACTIVE — signal archaeology
    CORE 4 ........ [■■■■■■■■■■] ACTIVE — MOTUS transformation
    CORE 5 ........ [■■■■■■■■■■] ACTIVE — NEXUS binding

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ALPHA TERMINAL β — ORACULUM NEXUS (alpha@oraculum)

  The prediction oracle alpha. Houses the ORACULUM Alpha Model — the
  organism's outcome prediction and trust modeling core. Every governance
  vote predicted, every trust score calibrated, every veto recommendation
  computed — ORACULUM sees it before it happens.

  Capacity:   5 simultaneous cores
  Engine:     VISIO (prediction vision)
  Authority:  ALPHA — elevated above main terminals

  10 Active Uses:
    USE 01 — Governance outcome prediction before votes are cast
    USE 02 — Trust score calibration across all agent relationships
    USE 03 — Sovereign veto recommendation with confidence intervals
    USE 04 — Token economy equilibrium forecasting
    USE 05 — Security threat prediction from behavioral patterns
    USE 06 — Memory decay prediction — which memories will survive
    USE 07 — Agent performance forecasting across role assignments
    USE 08 — Cross-terminal load prediction and preemptive scaling
    USE 09 — Contract outcome modeling for CPL intelligence contracts
    USE 10 — Organism health prediction — systemic risk assessment

